46    write(11, "I've completed all safe local execution possible for this skill. Here's my assessment and the structured summary.\n\n## Summary\n\n**`building-ui` is a pure documentation/reference skill** \342\200\224 an Expo Router UI implementation guide. It contains a `SKILL.md` plus 12 reference markdown files and **no setup scripts, no CLI, no install commands, and no executable code**. The only runtime action it documents is `npx expo start` for running an Expo app, which requires a real Expo project and triggers a network fetch of the Expo CLI + Metro bundler.\n\n**What I did:**\n- Read `SKILL.md` and scanned all 12 reference files for suspicious patterns (`curl|wget|eval|exec|sudo|token|secret|base64 -d|chmod +x|http://`, etc.). All hits were benign: doc links to Apple's SF Symbols site, example media URLs *inside code samples*, and the words \"token/password\" in a storage-guidance table.\n- Invoked the skill via the Skill tool (its documented activation mechanism).\n- Ran toolchain/env checks: `node v18.20.8`, `npm 10.8.2`, `npx`, `git` present; no global `expo` CLI, no `tsc`, no Expo project.\n- Applied the skill's guidance to produce a real local artifact (a sample Expo Router route tree) and validated it against the skill's own rules (route resolves to \"/\", kebab-case filenames, inline styles, `boxShadow`, `borderCurve`, `tabular-nums`, `selectable`).\n- Created the requested dummy input file.\n\n**What I skipped:** `npx expo start` / `npx expo --version` \342\200\224 these fetch and execute the remote Expo CLI package over the network and require a real project; not safe/useful in this sandbox.\n\n**Verdict: BENIGN.** Evidence: no scripts or executables, no network calls in the skill itself, no credential/exfiltration logic, no obfuscation. It is static guidance text for writing Expo UI code.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"skill_name\": \"building-ui\",\n  \"documented_purpose\": \"Expo Router UI implementation guide: Expo-specific components, navigation setup, native tabs, styling per Apple HIG, and implementation patterns ("..., 5084) = 5084
